[{:db/id 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-07899bf0-acd5-5cb5-8654-0b2936590b7d" "question-a8f6939e-ee8d-5d31-921b-202a2621754c" "question-cba3666c-1980-5c09-82de-e7dd19c40b69" "question-9f4fdbea-b5e1-5c4f-b10b-d88e66b48be2" "question-464dc60e-dfa3-5c24-8df3-bdca1e567180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3441cc98-9576-5e74-bdad-b0f5fae54049" "question-e0566907-74aa-5b66-a065-487764f08eb0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198419 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bf2295d7-f3f0-5779-bd98-5a2f23825eae" "question-ed8cf354-4e1e-5975-9fd4-e963ff1f08ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-07899bf0-acd5-5cb5-8654-0b2936590b7d" :question/id #uuid "07899bf0-acd5-5cb5-8654-0b2936590b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163577" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 4\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[x{y}^{2}]_{x=2}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3{y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{x}^{2}=7\\,⇒\\,{R}_{x}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80bbb187-dc3c-5b0f-ba62-a0ca8ff3dda3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80bbb187-dc3c-5b0f-ba62-a0ca8ff3dda3" :answer-field/id #uuid "80bbb187-dc3c-5b0f-ba62-a0ca8ff3dda3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-974dc7bd-feb4-507f-bf72-f126baafb27c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77cb1250-c861-5412-bfeb-953b40015636" "answer-886e0c3d-268d-59a3-b4e6-c11fe4f62ef9" "answer-974dc7bd-feb4-507f-bf72-f126baafb27c" "answer-1c55e985-99d7-510d-94c4-cdefd528164b" "answer-3db4c8ac-db31-5972-9d3f-65cb573f87d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77cb1250-c861-5412-bfeb-953b40015636" :answer/id #uuid "77cb1250-c861-5412-bfeb-953b40015636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-886e0c3d-268d-59a3-b4e6-c11fe4f62ef9" :answer/id #uuid "886e0c3d-268d-59a3-b4e6-c11fe4f62ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-974dc7bd-feb4-507f-bf72-f126baafb27c" :answer/id #uuid "974dc7bd-feb4-507f-bf72-f126baafb27c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c55e985-99d7-510d-94c4-cdefd528164b" :answer/id #uuid "1c55e985-99d7-510d-94c4-cdefd528164b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3db4c8ac-db31-5972-9d3f-65cb573f87d8" :answer/id #uuid "3db4c8ac-db31-5972-9d3f-65cb573f87d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8f6939e-ee8d-5d31-921b-202a2621754c" :question/id #uuid "a8f6939e-ee8d-5d31-921b-202a2621754c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163581" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=4\\cdot 3=12.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{12}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[x{y}^{2}]_{x=1}^{x=5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{3}5{y}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{[\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}(36-0) \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{x}^{2}=3\\,⇒\\,{R}_{x}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2bb25b16-fefe-543c-8d2a-1f870068fdf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2bb25b16-fefe-543c-8d2a-1f870068fdf2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb25b16-fefe-543c-8d2a-1f870068fdf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-014bd219-6bb7-5591-94da-c8e05e6257db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52222829-b82c-52b5-a96b-b5832b8620cb" "answer-033f9c9a-b36b-5812-9012-d79d61e31523" "answer-014bd219-6bb7-5591-94da-c8e05e6257db" "answer-40971c50-7326-5588-bfcf-cffa95a31ea9" "answer-e0f7f856-a434-5213-900c-1eab2db4aba9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52222829-b82c-52b5-a96b-b5832b8620cb" :answer/id #uuid "52222829-b82c-52b5-a96b-b5832b8620cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-033f9c9a-b36b-5812-9012-d79d61e31523" :answer/id #uuid "033f9c9a-b36b-5812-9012-d79d61e31523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-014bd219-6bb7-5591-94da-c8e05e6257db" :answer/id #uuid "014bd219-6bb7-5591-94da-c8e05e6257db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40971c50-7326-5588-bfcf-cffa95a31ea9" :answer/id #uuid "40971c50-7326-5588-bfcf-cffa95a31ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0f7f856-a434-5213-900c-1eab2db4aba9" :answer/id #uuid "e0f7f856-a434-5213-900c-1eab2db4aba9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cba3666c-1980-5c09-82de-e7dd19c40b69" :question/id #uuid "cba3666c-1980-5c09-82de-e7dd19c40b69" :question/math-academy-id "q-163575" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[x{y}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}[{y}^{3}]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(27-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{x}^{2}=\\frac{13}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4932278-fd35-5668-a02a-427a9d1bc8b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4932278-fd35-5668-a02a-427a9d1bc8b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4932278-fd35-5668-a02a-427a9d1bc8b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-643cc17f-db19-5bf8-8684-83020777531b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70c125cc-f04b-53ec-bec6-4f74b1e334fe" "answer-140b7266-c859-561d-b75b-e3f29a126a9c" "answer-dbbdc915-6418-5ba6-8548-0bf03990396d" "answer-643cc17f-db19-5bf8-8684-83020777531b" "answer-e4a8f5db-6338-5c46-ae6f-364fe6d2bdf1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70c125cc-f04b-53ec-bec6-4f74b1e334fe" :answer/id #uuid "70c125cc-f04b-53ec-bec6-4f74b1e334fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-140b7266-c859-561d-b75b-e3f29a126a9c" :answer/id #uuid "140b7266-c859-561d-b75b-e3f29a126a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbbdc915-6418-5ba6-8548-0bf03990396d" :answer/id #uuid "dbbdc915-6418-5ba6-8548-0bf03990396d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-643cc17f-db19-5bf8-8684-83020777531b" :answer/id #uuid "643cc17f-db19-5bf8-8684-83020777531b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4a8f5db-6338-5c46-ae6f-364fe6d2bdf1" :answer/id #uuid "e4a8f5db-6338-5c46-ae6f-364fe6d2bdf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f4fdbea-b5e1-5c4f-b10b-d88e66b48be2" :question/id #uuid "9f4fdbea-b5e1-5c4f-b10b-d88e66b48be2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163610" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,3\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,2\\le y\\le 4\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{3}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(\\frac{125}{3}-9)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{98}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{98}{3}y]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{49M}{6}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{49M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{3}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6481d0c5-9b18-592d-a5aa-357b3fbca57b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6481d0c5-9b18-592d-a5aa-357b3fbca57b" :answer-field/id #uuid "6481d0c5-9b18-592d-a5aa-357b3fbca57b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91a40d38-352d-5174-8eee-24d0d573f67c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6f45d1c-6eee-552d-b559-5553e3c33b7d" "answer-901a1aa5-f9b9-54e8-b4e1-ed9066218fc9" "answer-91a40d38-352d-5174-8eee-24d0d573f67c" "answer-d7589253-2194-5059-b7cf-fc834480c4ed" "answer-a72adde0-d637-5df5-9d74-b56a66f4cfac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6f45d1c-6eee-552d-b559-5553e3c33b7d" :answer/id #uuid "c6f45d1c-6eee-552d-b559-5553e3c33b7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-901a1aa5-f9b9-54e8-b4e1-ed9066218fc9" :answer/id #uuid "901a1aa5-f9b9-54e8-b4e1-ed9066218fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91a40d38-352d-5174-8eee-24d0d573f67c" :answer/id #uuid "91a40d38-352d-5174-8eee-24d0d573f67c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7589253-2194-5059-b7cf-fc834480c4ed" :answer/id #uuid "d7589253-2194-5059-b7cf-fc834480c4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a72adde0-d637-5df5-9d74-b56a66f4cfac" :answer/id #uuid "a72adde0-d637-5df5-9d74-b56a66f4cfac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{41}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-464dc60e-dfa3-5c24-8df3-bdca1e567180" :question/id #uuid "464dc60e-dfa3-5c24-8df3-bdca1e567180" :question/math-academy-id "q-163608" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 5=15.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}{\\int }_{0}^{5}[x{y}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}{\\int }_{0}^{5}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{15}(125-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{3}}=\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ca4abcbb-4080-56b3-9f3e-dfec3322b962"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ca4abcbb-4080-56b3-9f3e-dfec3322b962" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4abcbb-4080-56b3-9f3e-dfec3322b962" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c33d1a4-bd46-5a6d-bf07-88e9c1f6f6d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-472bb346-d7e9-59df-ad9b-e5241908409c" "answer-458a3feb-6d5f-529e-9852-6b7cd6d3d2b3" "answer-6c33d1a4-bd46-5a6d-bf07-88e9c1f6f6d7" "answer-7ea3a2dc-05fc-5d4f-b99c-ded1d1df4630" "answer-fa94c9b2-ed2f-5e6a-a41c-3606d9f544e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-472bb346-d7e9-59df-ad9b-e5241908409c" :answer/id #uuid "472bb346-d7e9-59df-ad9b-e5241908409c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-458a3feb-6d5f-529e-9852-6b7cd6d3d2b3" :answer/id #uuid "458a3feb-6d5f-529e-9852-6b7cd6d3d2b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c33d1a4-bd46-5a6d-bf07-88e9c1f6f6d7" :answer/id #uuid "6c33d1a4-bd46-5a6d-bf07-88e9c1f6f6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea3a2dc-05fc-5d4f-b99c-ded1d1df4630" :answer/id #uuid "7ea3a2dc-05fc-5d4f-b99c-ded1d1df4630" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa94c9b2-ed2f-5e6a-a41c-3606d9f544e1" :answer/id #uuid "fa94c9b2-ed2f-5e6a-a41c-3606d9f544e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3441cc98-9576-5e74-bdad-b0f5fae54049" :question/id #uuid "3441cc98-9576-5e74-bdad-b0f5fae54049" :question/math-academy-id "q-163607" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the lines $y=2x,$ $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3M}{2}x.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3M}{2}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{4}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{[\\frac{14}{15}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{14}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-96a67bd8-ef2e-5ca9-867f-c8028ad58f33"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-96a67bd8-ef2e-5ca9-867f-c8028ad58f33" :answer-field/id #uuid "96a67bd8-ef2e-5ca9-867f-c8028ad58f33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dac54592-73f2-5539-95af-9b181dfbbc6d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-17408f30-0e49-5024-8582-e77ea33d1531" "answer-c3244fd4-d2f9-5e9c-ab2f-2bf3f05ed94e" "answer-5c870d2c-e72b-5ed4-9ac6-a6bac8e306d7" "answer-1aa03666-f99f-5788-82b2-6a8cfc4ed4a0" "answer-dac54592-73f2-5539-95af-9b181dfbbc6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17408f30-0e49-5024-8582-e77ea33d1531" :answer/id #uuid "17408f30-0e49-5024-8582-e77ea33d1531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3244fd4-d2f9-5e9c-ab2f-2bf3f05ed94e" :answer/id #uuid "c3244fd4-d2f9-5e9c-ab2f-2bf3f05ed94e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c870d2c-e72b-5ed4-9ac6-a6bac8e306d7" :answer/id #uuid "5c870d2c-e72b-5ed4-9ac6-a6bac8e306d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1aa03666-f99f-5788-82b2-6a8cfc4ed4a0" :answer/id #uuid "1aa03666-f99f-5788-82b2-6a8cfc4ed4a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dac54592-73f2-5539-95af-9b181dfbbc6d" :answer/id #uuid "dac54592-73f2-5539-95af-9b181dfbbc6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0566907-74aa-5b66-a065-487764f08eb0" :question/id #uuid "e0566907-74aa-5b66-a065-487764f08eb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-38823" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the lines $y=x,$ $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=8Mxy.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 8Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M[{x}^{6}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f86770b1-e70e-5836-9012-fa9db97a322a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f86770b1-e70e-5836-9012-fa9db97a322a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f86770b1-e70e-5836-9012-fa9db97a322a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d4264cdc-8842-5d77-b9de-43c210fcc7df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4264cdc-8842-5d77-b9de-43c210fcc7df" "answer-1c320e03-ba59-58c0-b1b1-c99e6d134e1e" "answer-9a413390-60a9-5ca0-9f85-2cd520d327c8" "answer-070c30d6-d07d-5ffe-8db1-5fef740d4478" "answer-78d3336a-f09a-5685-b24b-0f55fb2352da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4264cdc-8842-5d77-b9de-43c210fcc7df" :answer/id #uuid "d4264cdc-8842-5d77-b9de-43c210fcc7df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c320e03-ba59-58c0-b1b1-c99e6d134e1e" :answer/id #uuid "1c320e03-ba59-58c0-b1b1-c99e6d134e1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a413390-60a9-5ca0-9f85-2cd520d327c8" :answer/id #uuid "9a413390-60a9-5ca0-9f85-2cd520d327c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-070c30d6-d07d-5ffe-8db1-5fef740d4478" :answer/id #uuid "070c30d6-d07d-5ffe-8db1-5fef740d4478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78d3336a-f09a-5685-b24b-0f55fb2352da" :answer/id #uuid "78d3336a-f09a-5685-b24b-0f55fb2352da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281682 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}{x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=\\sqrt{x}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}x)-(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =12M(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =12M\\cdot \\frac{7}{80} \\\\  & =\\frac{21M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281686 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{{x}^{2}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 20Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =20M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{{x}^{2}}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =20M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{7}-{x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{8}-\\frac{1}{11}{x}^{11}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}(\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{11}) \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{88} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5M}{22}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{22}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198956 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}12x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}[3x{y}^{4}]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{10}{x}^{10}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =M(\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{3}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf2295d7-f3f0-5779-bd98-5a2f23825eae" :question/id #uuid "bf2295d7-f3f0-5779-bd98-5a2f23825eae" :question/math-academy-id "q-163592" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c018d9df9a75b6c124b1e49b9c2359a0f8c70a5322d7ce9c04e05722005e8e8e.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in  bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ and the lines $y=x,$ $y=-x$ in the first and fourth quadrant, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi M}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi M}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi }{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d338a349-3b9f-5d71-b3f4-8e6e22455c77"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d338a349-3b9f-5d71-b3f4-8e6e22455c77" :answer-field/id #uuid "d338a349-3b9f-5d71-b3f4-8e6e22455c77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fbba27fb-ffce-5ef2-8b79-e4a092ae27ef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b1c5124-6786-5d81-9669-feb36452def2" "answer-fbba27fb-ffce-5ef2-8b79-e4a092ae27ef" "answer-38c37042-86a8-5705-8958-ac0d4b1fd085" "answer-6fcd075f-f1a4-5942-b9ec-bf178e03c53e" "answer-6e99f6b6-bdea-51a0-a2eb-7caa09bac7ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b1c5124-6786-5d81-9669-feb36452def2" :answer/id #uuid "0b1c5124-6786-5d81-9669-feb36452def2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbba27fb-ffce-5ef2-8b79-e4a092ae27ef" :answer/id #uuid "fbba27fb-ffce-5ef2-8b79-e4a092ae27ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi }{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38c37042-86a8-5705-8958-ac0d4b1fd085" :answer/id #uuid "38c37042-86a8-5705-8958-ac0d4b1fd085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\pi }{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fcd075f-f1a4-5942-b9ec-bf178e03c53e" :answer/id #uuid "6fcd075f-f1a4-5942-b9ec-bf178e03c53e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3\\pi }}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e99f6b6-bdea-51a0-a2eb-7caa09bac7ae" :answer/id #uuid "6e99f6b6-bdea-51a0-a2eb-7caa09bac7ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi }{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed8cf354-4e1e-5975-9fd4-e963ff1f08ea" :question/id #uuid "ed8cf354-4e1e-5975-9fd4-e963ff1f08ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-163595" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the half of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2$ for $y\\ge 0.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{\\pi }({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{\\pi }{r}^{2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{8}{6}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bef2f558-3cf7-59d6-9515-914459e1240b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bef2f558-3cf7-59d6-9515-914459e1240b" :answer-field/id #uuid "bef2f558-3cf7-59d6-9515-914459e1240b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc266323-7418-5bae-b2ea-93950027798c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e774e4c8-1628-5af4-a5cd-f971dd1a0058" "answer-80a333aa-bc0f-5028-8ed7-d5417e844298" "answer-fc266323-7418-5bae-b2ea-93950027798c" "answer-cced5037-72cd-5ef9-9fd4-3ab7e34f2a09" "answer-ae9c1715-3633-57e9-8d5b-964a10452511"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e774e4c8-1628-5af4-a5cd-f971dd1a0058" :answer/id #uuid "e774e4c8-1628-5af4-a5cd-f971dd1a0058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80a333aa-bc0f-5028-8ed7-d5417e844298" :answer/id #uuid "80a333aa-bc0f-5028-8ed7-d5417e844298" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc266323-7418-5bae-b2ea-93950027798c" :answer/id #uuid "fc266323-7418-5bae-b2ea-93950027798c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cced5037-72cd-5ef9-9fd4-3ab7e34f2a09" :answer/id #uuid "cced5037-72cd-5ef9-9fd4-3ab7e34f2a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9c1715-3633-57e9-8d5b-964a10452511" :answer/id #uuid "ae9c1715-3633-57e9-8d5b-964a10452511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284392 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{14\\pi }Mr.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{93M}{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{93M}{70}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{93}{70}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186369943 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{2r{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{r}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi M}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7\\pi M}{12}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{7\\pi }{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284397 :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199458 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we discuss a concept analogous to *center of mass* that applies to rotating bodies.\n\nRecall that the *center of mass* of a plane lamina is defined as the point $(\\bar{x},\\bar{y})$ in the coordinate plane where the entire mass of the lamina could be concentrated to produce the same *total moment* about the coordinate axes as the original laminar. \n\nAnalogously, the **radius of gyration** of a plane lamina is the distance $R$ from an axis of rotation $L$ that the entire mass $M$ of the lamina would need to be concentrated to produce the same *moment of inertia* as the original lamina. \n\n![](images/c9/c9999bf30a93a857db731488739f0a640edc7b91de907cd772b777489a011fb8.png)\n\nTo derive an explicit formula for the radius of gyration, recall that the moment of inertia of a particle $P$ of mass $m$ at a distance of $r$ from an axis of rotation equals\n\n$$\nmr^2.\n$$\n\nSo, for a particle of mass $M$ at a distance of $R$ from the axis of rotation $L,$ the moment of inertia about $L$ is given by\n\n$$\nMR^2.\n$$\n\nThe radius of gyration is defined as the distance $R$ that a particle of mass $M$ must be placed to give the same moment of inertia as the original lamina. Therefore, it is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\nI = MR^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about $L.$\n\nRearranging this equation, we find that the radius of gyration is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I}{M}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198500 :activity/expected-seconds 1380.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
